  "_meta": {
    "description": "Aggregated 20-sector direct requirements matrix A. Element A[i,j] = USD of input from sector i required to produce 1 USD of output by sector j. Row i = supplier; Column j = customer. Aggregated/calibrated from EXIOBASE-3 Multi-Regional Input-Output (MRIO) world totals (2019). Used by Layer 3 (network propagation) to compute total cost shocks via the Leontief inverse L = (I - A)^-1. Reference SCREENING level \u2014 full MRIO requires sub-licensed EXIOBASE / WIOD / OECD ICIO data.",
    "sources": [
      "Stadler, Wood, Bulavskaya et al. (2018). 'EXIOBASE 3: Developing a Time Series of Detailed Environmentally Extended Multi-Regional Input-Output Tables.' Journal of Industrial Ecology 22(3): 502-515. https://doi.org/10.1111/jiec.12715",
      "Lenzen, Kanemoto, Moran, Geschke (2012). 'Mapping the Structure of the World Economy.' Environmental Science & Technology 46(15): 8374-8381 (WIOD methodology)",
      "Acemoglu, Carvalho, Ozdaglar, Tahbaz-Salehi (2012). 'The Network Origins of Aggregate Fluctuations.' Econometrica 80(5): 1977-2016 \u2014 theoretical basis",
      "Reisch, Diem, Pichler, Stangl, Thurner (2025). 'Combined climate stress testing of supply-chain networks and the financial system.' arXiv:2503.10644 \u2014 methodology for cascade modelling"
    ],
    "method": "Leontief: x = (I-A)^-1 * f. For shock vector s (sectoral cost shock as fraction of output), total cost impact on sector j = sum_i L[i,j] * s[i]. Substitution elasticity (Cobb-Douglas baseline = 1.0) can be applied via softmax-tempered Leontief.",
